  "consumers": "tests/fixtures/native-sync-io-clients",
  "checks": [
    "Ordinary and reviewed packages expose the same six immediate-value declarations and one compiler-discovered filesystem capability; no selected task, iterator or host import.",
    "Both clients demonstrate ordered BaseIO reference mutation, real filesystem IO, invalid-input refusal, a subsequent successful call, and four combinations of returned versus thrown structured Except values. The owned UTF-8 payload survives disposal of the Lean result.",
    "A cold invalid argument does not run the component initializer. A valid call runs it once and the broker's live identity count returns to baseline. C exports no start/poll for the checked entry. Python imports no asyncio, takes no binding context, and refuses worker-thread and post-initialization fork calls without poisoning the parent.",
    "The C executable uses the relocated archive and pkg-config with the build tree removed. CPython installs offline from the handoff's two wheels. Neither deployed caller has Lean tools on PATH."
  ],
  "boundary": "These two synchronous profiles do not add structured transport for the internal IO.Error constructors; ordinary IO carries a message (plus the declaration in Python), while EIO retains its declared payload. The shared native runtime still performs its normal startup. No adapter-created task or host event loop delivers these calls. These receipts do not cover other targets or close VO #1222.",
  "controls": [
    "With freshly compiled source, omitting the required filesystem grant, selecting only a pure companion, or returning an unselected Task each fails for its own diagnostic before a handoff exists.",
    "An in-memory BaseIO/EIO selection builds with nativeEffects: [] and no capability in the IR even when the module defines unrelated file IO.",
    "The existing host-object-installed regression also built and pip-installed two components with the same shared runtime. Both routes retained their 19 scalar/typed-result conversions, original exceptions, reentry and cleanup. This is a mixed-profile regression, not additional standalone-target evidence."
  ],
  "reproduce": {
    "build": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_TEST=1 LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_EVIDENCE=/absolute/path/to/new-releases node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-sync-io.mjs",
    "replay": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_REPLAY=/absolute/path/to/original-releases LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_EXPECTED=docs/evidence/native-sync-io-20261122.json node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-sync-io.mjs",
    "mixedProfileRegression": "LEAN_BRIDGE_HOST_OBJECT_TEST=1 LEAN_BRIDGE_HOST_PYTHON=/absolute/path/to/python3 node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/host-object-installed.mjs",
    "tools": "For builds, point LEAN_BRIDGE_LEAN_PREFIX and LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON at the pinned toolchains and provide a C compiler, CMake, pkg-config and CPython headers. Installed replay only needs the consumer tools and the original handoffs."
  },
